## Regression found in final audit
The telemetry/multi-query integration had replaced `hermes-mission-worker.mjs` with a version that unintentionally removed two existing Forge v3 reliability guards:
- bounded local Kernel requests (`AbortSignal.timeout`, default 60s);
- preservation of the real worker/adapter failure when reporting that failure back to the Kernel itself fails.

That regression could leave a worker pending indefinitely if the local Kernel accepted a connection but never answered, preventing the one-click runtime from clearing/retrying the active run.

## Fix
- restore `DEFAULT_KERNEL_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS` and the bounded `kernelRequest` wrapper;
- keep the new search telemetry payload unchanged;
- restore reconciliation through the bounded request wrapper;
- restore `reported: true/false` and sanitized `reportError` semantics;
- restore the lost regression tests for stalled Kernel calls, stalled claim, rejected failure report and unreachable failure report;
- retain all telemetry tests.

## Guardrails
- only `apps/local-kernel/hermes-mission-worker.mjs` and its test changed;
- Forge renderer/spider/anvil/canvas untouched;
- `packages/kernel/src/evidence/support.ts` untouched;
- search planning/selection logic untouched;
- no `main` changes;
- no force-push;
- `publicLaunchApproved=false`.

Integration status: all commits from this proposal are now contained in main through merged consolidation #254 (79ebdb1eb609ba05d3a1574d52b1e2e30a0b9562). Closed as incorporated; the branch is preserved. Internal baseline only; authentic Hermes acceptance and installed-PC UAT remain outstanding.

